{% comment %}
  Outputs the handle of the collection that represents a class product's
  teacher, or nothing when there is no match. Capture it and look the
  collection up in the caller:

    {%- capture th -%}{%- render 'rb-teacher-handle', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign th = th | strip -%}
    {%- assign teacher_col = collections[th] -%}

  Why a lookup at all: one class template serves every class, so the teacher
  band and the hero portrait have to come from the product rather than from a
  per-page setting.

  This store models a teacher as a collection holding that teacher's classes,
  so the product already belongs to it. Two passes, in order of confidence:

    1. a collection whose title is the instructor's — matched on the surname
       rather than the whole string, because the catalogue is not consistent:
       the class credits "Zara Farinha" while her collections read "Zara-Leigh
       Farinha", and "Shelly Cowling" is missing an e against "Shelley
       Cowling". Both still land on the right person by surname;
    2. failing that, any collection whose handle looks like a teacher's
       (teacher-1 … teacher-15), excluding the "teachers" index collection
       itself, which every class also belongs to.

  Someone who both teaches and exhibits has TWO collections under one title —
  the teacher one and the artist one — and the store's convention is that the
  teacher's handle carries a "-1" suffix (susan-orpen-1 beside susan-orpen).
  That suffix decides the tie; without it the first match wins, which is still
  the same person's page either way.

  Accepts: product.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign instr = product.metafields.booking.instructor_name | downcase | strip
  assign name_parts = instr | split: ' '
  assign surname = name_parts | last

  assign found = ''
  assign fallback = ''

  if instr != blank
    for c in product.collections
      assign ct = c.title | downcase | strip
      assign hit = false
      if ct == instr
        assign hit = true
      elsif surname != blank and ct contains surname
        assign hit = true
      endif

      if hit
        assign tail = c.handle | slice: -2, 2
        if tail == '-1' and found == blank
          assign found = c.handle
        elsif fallback == blank
          assign fallback = c.handle
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if found == blank
    assign found = fallback
  endif

  if found == blank
    for c in product.collections
      if c.handle == 'teachers'
        continue
      endif
      if c.handle contains 'teacher'
        assign found = c.handle
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  echo found
-%}
